    "title": "Local crafter brings Texas-sized 'The Three' homecoming mum to KBTX - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Desiree Ibarra ,\n5 hours ago BRYAN, Texas (KBTX) - Texas homecoming season is officially underway, bringing with it the state’s massive, glitter-filled tradition of homecoming mums. Local mum maker Connie Wawarofsky, owner of The Southern Cottage, shared the history of the craft, which migrated from Missouri to Baylor University in 1936. During her appearance, Connie taught hosts Crystal Galny and Conner Beene the tedious process of building a garter—complete with the “chop and drop” steps of prepping the mum—before revealing a massive surprise: a Texas-sized custom “The Three” mum. Read full article",
